# Wave W17-S (Route 127): kelp sand — kelp-shadowed shore sand: a warm shore sand standing in the kelp forest\u2019s shallows, green shadow-flecks lying across the tread where the fronds above shade the bottom (design: the trench drops to a kelp forest no net has ever mapped — even the lane\u2019s shore sand carries the forest\u2019s shadow). Route 127\u2019s own sand — the fleet\u2019s only green-shadowed sand: split from Route 125\u2019s bright tide-banded sand by the kelp flecks and the missing tide lines, and from Route 128\u2019s sparse deep-channel sand by warmth and cover.
